{"availability":"available","full":"ctom2/colie","name":"colie","description":"[ECCV 2024] This is the official code for the paper \"Fast Context-Based Low-Light Image Enhancement via Neural Implicit Representations\"","category":"Developer tools","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":86,"forks":6,"created":"2024-03-12T09:55:58Z","updated":"2025-11-06T13:11:50Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["computer-vision","image-enhancement","low-light-image-enhancement","neural-implicit-representations","self-supervised","zero-shot"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/chobola/colie","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:14.696Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:14.696Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:14.696Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:14.696Z","stars":86,"forks":6}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":[],"features":["Challenges with Current Methods: Existing deep learning methods for low-light image enhancement struggle with high-resolution images, and they often fail to meet practical visual perception needs in diverse, unseen…","Introduction of CoLIE: CoLIE (Context-Based Low-Light Image Enhancement) is a novel approach for enhancing low-light images. It works by mapping 2D coordinates of underexposed images to their illumination components,…","Methodology: The method utilizes HSV color space for image reconstruction. It employs an implicit neural function along with an embedded guided filter to further reduce computational overhead.","Innovations in Training: CoLIE introduces a single image-based training loss function. This function aims to improve the model's adaptability across various scenes, enhancing its practical applicability."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ctom2/colie/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f30fdd20b1e270aa78c71fb57028fd31ad6ba084e1387dac1108d1e6aee4fb66","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:14.843Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:14